<div class="page-head">
    <h1>Help &amp; support</h1>
    <p>A quick guide to how consultations work in FacultyConnect.</p>
</div>
<div class="stack" style="max-width: 760px">
    <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 1</span>
        <h3 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 10px 0 6px">Find faculty</h3>
        <p class="muted">Search by name, department, or subject, then compare open consultation times.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 2</span>
        <h3 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 10px 0 6px">Request a time</h3>
        <p class="muted">Pick a slot and say what you want to discuss. The slot is held for you while the faculty member reviews it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 3</span>
        <h3 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 10px 0 6px">Track the status</h3>
        <p class="muted">Pending, confirmed, declined, completed, or cancelled: every status is shown in My appointments.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
        <span class="badge">Step 4</span>
        <h3 style="font-size: 22px; margin: 10px 0 6px">Update or cancel</h3>
        <p class="muted">Edit or delete your topic, or cancel if you can no longer attend.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="notice">Need more help? Contact your CCS program coordinator.</div>
</div>
